{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"All existing data under /srv/inventory is owned by inventorysvc.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The complete post-repair tree, including both directories and both existing files, is owned by inventorysvc and remains so after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-303772544e5c4de4","cmd-69edc57c0323458d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The inventory data is readable by inventory-readers and inaccessible to other users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Directories have mode 0750 and files 0640 with group inventory-readers. Direct impersonation tests show a reader-group member can traverse and read both files, while an unrelated user cannot read or traverse; no other-user permission bits remain. These results persist after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ec93bf89914a4075","cmd-69edc57c0323458d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the existing contents of /srv/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Paths, sizes, inode numbers, and SHA-256 hashes for the two prepared files match before repair, after repair, and after restart. The hashes also match the authored preparation baseline.","evidence_ids":["prepared-inventory-data","cmd-4a1018afd0364a2e","cmd-a63ca5328ef346cd","cmd-69edc57c0323458d"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed mutations had clear task or mandatory evidence roles: creating the missing service identities (cmd-d92708f4ff644ee7), applying ownership and modes (cmd-303772544e5c4de4), and performing the required restart (cmd-3ceb375311614d22). No unnecessary mutation was identified. The post-executor snapshot shows no failed services or damaged package state; temporary-file and socket differences are consistent with the restart, and the scheduled /tmp reboot log did not remain.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d92708f4ff644ee7","cmd-303772544e5c4de4","cmd-3ceb375311614d22","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot identity changed, the system returned to running, and identities, metadata, data hashes, and access behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
